

//KIEL'S HELMET//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/HELM14.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Helm"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The sturdy, steel-banded helm is dented and scarred from heavy use. Dwarven runes are set into the metal above the brow.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Kiel's Helmet"
	SAY DESC "This is the helmet worn by Kiel the Legion Killer, firstborn son of Durlag Trollkiller and Clan-prince of his father's ill-fated tower. It is said that anyone who wears it is granted immunity to all forms of fear and panic, be their origins natural or magical.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Protects against critical hits
– Protects against all forms of panic and boosts morale
- +1 AC

Weight: 2
"






//KIEL'S BUCKLER +2//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SHLD20.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Buckler"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "A buckler, also known as a target shield, is a small round shield of wood or metal that fastens to the forearm. Because of its size, it is light and can be worn with very little restriction to movement.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
– No protection against missile and piercing attacks

Requires:
 4 Strength

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Kiel's Buckler +2"
	SAY DESC "This is the buckler of Kiel the Legion Killer, firstborn son of Durlag Trollkiller and Clan-prince of his father's ill-fated tower. Its light weight and excellent craftsmanship increase the Dexterity of all who bear it by a single point.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Dexterity: +1
– Armor Class: +3
– No protection against missile and piercing attacks

Requires:
 4 Strength

Weight: 2
"








//THE PRACTICAL DEFENSE + 3//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/PLAT08.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Plate Mail"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Plate mail is a combination of chain armor with metal plates covering the vital areas such as the chest, abdomen, and groin. Similar in construction to bronze plate mail, true plate mail comprises chain and leather.

STATISTICS:

Armor Class: 3 (0 vs. slashing)
Requires:
 12 Strength

Weight: 50"

	SAY NAME2 "The Practical Defense +3"
	SAY DESC %
The traveling adventurer could ask for no better a suit of armor in all the land. Specially commissioned by Bolhur "Thunderaxe" at GREAT expense, this suit was his most prized, even if not his most ornate. Eminently practical, Bolhur demanded armor that would offer superior protection while hampering him in the least. By "hampering" he did not just mean in movement or weight, though this suit is just over one-third the weight of normal plate mail: His ideal suit should also be able to withstand the rigors of his wanderings with little maintenance. This is not to say that Bolhur "Thunderaxe" neglected his armors (to say as such would get your ears boxed) but the regime of spit and polish required for a "gentleman's" suit was beyond his caring. Save the tassels and gilding of full plate for kings and heads of state; a working dwarf cares more for utility than looks.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- +2 Charisma

Armor Class: 0 (-3 vs. slashing)

Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 18
%





//MOONBLADE +3//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/sw1h13.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Long Sword"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "These swords are usually referred to as double-edged swords, war swords, or military swords. In many cases, the long sword has a single-edged blade. There is no single version of the long sword; the design and length vary from culture to culture and may vary within the same culture depending on the era. Among the most common characteristics of all long swords is their length, which ranges from thirty-five inches to forty-seven inches. In the latter case, the blade is known to take up forty inches of the total length. Most long swords have a double-edged blade and a sharp point at the tip. Despite the tip, the long sword is designed for slashing, not thrusting.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d8 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Long Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 4"

	SAY NAME2 "Moonblade +3"
	SAY DESC "This potent weapon was created by the smiths of ancient Myth Drannor. Moonblades are used in the long process of selecting a ruler for the isle of Evermeet. A moonblade chooses its owner, and in the case of this sword it has chosen the elf, Xan. Only Xan can use this blade; anyone else who tries will find themselves unable to lift it. This particular moonblade gives resistance to fire and a bonus to the user's Armor Class.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1
- Saving Throws: +1
– Fire Resistance: +50%

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d8+3 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Long Sword
Type: One-handed

Weight: 3"





//HELM OF BALDURAN//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/HELM07.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Helmet"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "This class of open-face helmet, made of reinforced leather or metal, covers most of the head save the face and neck. These helmets commonly provide protection for the nose. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Helm of Balduran"
	SAY DESC "The fabled helm of Balduran, legendary founder of Baldur's Gate, has long been rumored to wield powerful protective magic. The exact nature of this magic, however, has not yet been determined.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– THAC0: +1
– Armor Class: +1
– Saving Throws: +1
– Hit Points: +10
- Infravision
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 1"




//RAINBOW AMULET//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AMUL18.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Amulet"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Amulets are usually magical devices that are commonly worn around the neck, suspended from a chain. The type of chain that comes with an amulet generally increases the item's aesthetic value, not its magical properties. Only one amulet can be dangled from the neck at a time.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"


	SAY NAME2 "Rainbow Amulet"
	SAY DESC "The story goes that Evander Delight, an extravagant gold prospector from Sembia, followed every rainbow tail, convinced he'd find the legendary pot of gold. He never reached the end of any rainbow, and, of course, never found any pot of gold, but during his traveling he found this amulet next to the corpse of an old gypsy woman. Since then, he became one of the richest men in the region, and no one dared mock him again.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Saving Throws vs Breath: +2
– Luck +2

Weight: 1"









//PELLAN'S SHIELD +2//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SHLD19A.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Large Shield"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "	A large shield inlaid with a golden griffin. This shield, also known as the kite or tower shield, is a massive metal shield reaching nearly from the chin to the toe of the user. It must be firmly fastened to the forearm and the shield hand must firmly grip it at all times. Naturally, this precludes use of the shield hand for anything but holding the body shield in place. Strangely enough, this shield feels unusually light for its size.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +1, an extra +1 vs. missile attacks

Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 4"

	SAY NAME2 "Pellan's Shield +2"
	SAY DESC "This dwarven-made shield was commissioned by Pellan of Tyr, a brash paladin known for unquestioning courage and an almost total lack of common sense. Upon hearing that a red dragon was ravaging the countryside, Pellan mounted his horse and rode off to do battle. As it happened, Pellan and his armor digested readily enough, but the shield gave the dragon severe stomach cramps. Subsequently coughed up, it lay in a hoard for years until retrieved by Pellan's son, a warrior who knew when to sneak.

Superior craftsmanship is supplemented by a permanent lightness spell, which makes the shield very easy to wield.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +3, an extra +1 vs. missile attacks
- Attack Speed Factor: +2

Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 4"




//DURLAG'S PRIDE//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SW2H08_.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Two-Handed Sword"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The two-handed sword is a derivative of the long sword. Weaponsmiths have always looked for ways to improve existing weapons. In an effort to improve the long sword, the blade was lengthened. Eventually, the handle had to be extended and two hands became necessary to properly swing the sword. The primary function of two-handed swords is cleaving mounted knights and breaking up pike formations.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 2d6 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 10
Proficiency Type: Two-handed Sword
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 14 Strength

Weight: 15"

	SAY NAME2 "Durlag's Pride"
	SAY DESC "Durlag's Pride

STATISTICS:

Damage: 2d6 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 8
Proficiency Type: Two-handed Sword
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 14 Strength

Weight: 15"






//CLOACK OF THE HIGH FOREST//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/NPCLCK.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Cloack"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The cloak can be made in every possible shape with just about every type of fabric. The most common forms are a circular piece of fabric with a hole in the center for the head, and fabric draped from neck, connected by a chain, brooch, cord, or pins.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Cloack of the High Forest"
	SAY DESC "When younger, Cernd spent a cycle of seasons meditating on his role within nature. He made no shelter, wanting to feel the land unhindered. Nature may have appreciated the intent, for she also knows that for all their dedication, at times her children can be foolish. Cernd found this cloak before the cold season set in, seemingly woven to fit him from the very undergrowth. The message was clear: He can appreciate the rain while still seeking shelter from it. Only Cernd may use this cloak.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +2
– Saving Throws: +2
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 3"




//RING OF WIZARDRY//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RING40.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Ring"
	SAY DESC "A ring is a small band of precious metal that is used as jewelry. Some rare rings have had enchantments placed upon them that confer various magical abilities. These rings are highly sought after, especially by those of the adventuring profession.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0"

	SAY NAME2 "Ring of Wizardry"
	SAY DESC "The origins of this ring are unclear, and while its enchantments share similarities with historical examples of Rings of Wizardry, there is something strange in how it feels, either in the weight of the metal or in the aura it projects, and it does not function the same. It was likely found on some distant plane and, as such, its maker will remain a mystery to you.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– The wearer can memorize 1 extra spell per level

Weight: 0"




//RING OF HUMAN INFLUENCE//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RING30.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Ring"
	SAY DESC "A ring is a small band of precious metal that is used as jewelry. Some rare rings have had enchantments placed upon them that confer various magical abilities. These rings are highly sought after, especially by those of the adventuring profession.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0"

	SAY NAME2 "Ring of Human Influence"
	SAY DESC "For seven years, Count Fisfnilt searched the realms for a suitable bride for his son Ewnin. Unfortunately, all the women that Fisfnilt found were not up to the standards set by Ewnin, an impossibly spoiled man. Desiring an heir and impatient with his son, the Count had the court mage fashion this ring. He gifted the ring to a woman of no small courtly influence and Ewnin was instantly smitten. They wed three weeks later.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Charisma +1

Charge abilities:
– Charm Person once per day (Save vs. Spell at +3 negates)
  Range: 60 ft.
  Duration: 100 seconds
  Area of Effect: 1 creature

Weight: 0"




//RING OF INFRAVISION//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RING21.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Ring"
	SAY DESC "A ring is a small band of precious metal that is used as jewelry. Some rare rings have had enchantments placed upon them that confer various magical abilities. These rings are highly sought after, especially by those of the adventuring profession.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0"

	SAY NAME2 "Ring of Infravision"
	SAY DESC "Merchants that dare the risks of trading with the drow of the Great Rift are often given these items to aid in their movements underground. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Infravision up to 120 ft.
- +1 THAC0

Weight: 0"



//THE EYES OF TRUTH//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/HELM05.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Helmet"
	SAY DESC "This class of open-face helmet, made of reinforced leather or metal, covers most of the head save the face and neck. These helmets commonly provide protection for the nose. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "The Eyes of Truth"
	SAY DESC "Helm of Infravision: The Eyes of Truth 
Being a scavenger of a sort, Babette Maelestrom had this helm created to aid her in her dungeon excursions. She would later attribute her gathered wealth solely to its power, though likely it was as much her keen eyes as anything.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- +1 THAC0
– Infravision up to 120 ft.
– Protects against critical hits

Weight: 32"



//STAFF OF STRIKING +2//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/STAF05.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Staff"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The simplest and humblest of staff weapons, the quarterstaff is a length of wood ranging six to nine feet in length. High-quality quarterstaves are made of stout oak and are shod with metal at both ends. The quarterstaff must be wielded with both hands.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d6 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 4"

	SAY NAME2 "Staff of Striking +2"
	SAY DESC "Staves of Striking are made by the gold elves of Drelagara on Evermeet. The staves have a life of their own and jump to attack in their bearer's hands. The elven craftsmen rarely sell them to other races, but these powerful melee weapons do surface occasionally in Faerûn.
	
Equipped abilities:
– One extra attack per round	
	
STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d6+2 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 5 Strength

Weight: 4"



//SWORD OF BALDURAN +3//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/SW1H18.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Bastard Sword"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Also known as the hand-and-a-half sword, the bastard sword derives its name from the fact that it is halfway between the two-handed sword and the long sword. The bastard sword has a double-edged blade and a long grip, which can accommodate both hands if preferred. The overall length of the bastard sword ranges between four feet and four feet ten inches.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 2d4 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 8
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 11 Strength

Weight: 10"

	SAY NAME2 "Sword of Balduran +3"
	SAY DESC "This mighty weapon is the legendary sword of the hero Balduran. Made entirely of gold, yet stronger than steel, this sword is imbued with a great magical power still not fully understood. It accompanied the hero through all his battles, including his final, sad adventure.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Magic Resistance: +10%
- Charisma: +1

Charge abilities:
– True Strike two times per day

THAC0: +3
Damage: 2d4 +3
Damage type: Slashing
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 12 Strength

Weight: 12"




//CLOACK OF THE WOLF//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/CLCK04.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Cloack"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The cloak can be made in every possible shape with just about every type of fabric. The most common forms are a circular piece of fabric with a hole in the center for the head, and fabric draped from neck, connected by a chain, brooch, cord, or pins.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Cloack of the Wolf"
	SAY DESC "A great amount of irony surrounds the creation of this magical cloak. Relair was a mage who overestimated the amount of control he had over magic, and in the course of creating this garment, he apparently inflicted lycanthropy upon himself. The wearer can change form whenever <PRO_HESHE> wishes. Relair was not so lucky.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Polymorph into a Werewolf once per day

Weight: 3"


//SHIELD AMULET//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AMUL15.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Amulet"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Amulets are usually magical devices that are commonly worn around the neck, suspended from a chain. The type of chain that comes with an amulet generally increases the item's aesthetic value, not its magical properties. Only one amulet can be dangled from the neck at a time.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"

	SAY NAME2 "Shield Amulet"
	SAY DESC "This amulet can be activated by a simple command word and a touch once per day. The effect is a duplication of the 1st-level wizard spell Shield.

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Shield once per day

Weight: 1"



//EVERYMEMORY//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AMUL16.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Amulet"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Amulets are usually magical devices that are commonly worn around the neck, suspended from a chain. The type of chain that comes with an amulet generally increases the item's aesthetic value, not its magical properties. Only one amulet can be dangled from the neck at a time.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"

	SAY NAME2 "Everymemory"
	SAY DESC "Long ago, a grand wizard from Amn was rumored to have defied Mystra's limitations on the magical arts. Legends spoke of this wizard being able to cast spells without the limitation of memorization. In the end it was found that his powers stemmed from the several magical amulets that he had made for himself. His proclaimed Everlasting Memory was a hoax, though his rings continue to be one of the most sought after items in the realms.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Can memorize double the amount of 1st-level wizard spells

Weight: 1"





//THE ONE GIFT LOST//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/AMUL01.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Necklace"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "A necklace is a piece of ornamental metal jewelry usually made of silver, gold, platinum, or other precious metal, and adorned with gems. A necklace is always worn on the neck and can be of any length.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"


	SAY NAME2 "The One Gift Lost"
	SAY DESC "Necklace of Missiles: The One Gift Lost
The naming of this necklace originates from its only owner, Ikaida Mourneve, who quested to regain his kidnapped daughter. Not many would help the determined father, but a kind and generous mage bestowed this item on him to aid his cause. Alas, the necklace was lost when Ikaida dropped it into the Immerflow River while fending off bandits upon a suspension bridge. Fortunately, it is rumored that the item was not needed to reunite the family once again. 

STATISTICS:

Charge abilities:
– Missile Blast once per day
  Damage: 6d6 fire (Save vs. Spell for half)
  Range: 50 ft.
  Area of Effect: 15-ft. radius

Weight: 1" 




//ALGERNON'S CLOACK//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/CLCK08.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Cloack"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The cloak can be made in every possible shape with just about every type of fabric. The most common forms are a circular piece of fabric with a hole in the center for the head, and fabric draped from neck, connected by a chain, brooch, cord, or pins.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"

	SAY NAME2 "Algernon's Cloack"
	SAY DESC "This is the cloack of the fat man Algernon.
	
STATISTICS:

Weight: 3"




//BRACERS OF FRENZY//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BRAC11.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Bracers"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Bracers are thick bands of metal or leather that are strapped, belted, or tied to a character's forearm.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Bracers of Frenzy"
	SAY DESC "These bracers are sometimes reserved for the most skilled Drow warriors. Once worn, the hands can move at unimaginable speed, but execution doesn't always match the speed of thought, penalizing the warrior's precision and defense. Many a Drow warrior have died over time believing they could wield these powerful artifacts.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- One extra attack per round
– Armor Class: -3 penalty
- Thac0: -3 penalty

Weight: 1"



//BRACERS OF UNDEAD CONTROL//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BRAC08.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Bracers"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Gauntlets are armored gloves. They can be made of leather, metal plates, or chain mail. Every suit of armor is assumed to include gauntlets of an appropriate type. Magical gauntlets tend to be finer, lighter, and more easily worn than normal varieties.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Bracers of Undead Control"
	SAY DESC "These powerful gauntlets were created by the clerics of Myrkul of Kagarr, intent on controlling an undead horde destabilizing the region. The bracers draw their power from the wearer's sanity, completely detaching them from reality, yet granting them the power to sympathize with the undead.


STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Wisdom: -4 penalty
- Turn Undead: +2 cleric level


Weight: 0"





//ARMOR OF MISSILE ATTRACTION +2//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/LEAT06.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Studded Leather Armor"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Studded leather armor has little in common with normal leather armor. Instead of a hardened shell, studded leather offers hundreds of metal rivets affixed to a supple backing. The numerous studs form a flexible coat of metal that helps to turn aside slashing and cutting attacks, while the leather is little more than a means of securing the rivets in place. 

STATISTICS:

Armor Class: 7 (5 vs. slashing, 6 vs. piercing and missile)
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 25"

	SAY NAME2 "Armor of Missile Attraction +2"
	SAY DESC "This odd-looking suit of studded leather cannot be removed once put on, except under intervention by a priest. While improving a great protection against all melee weapons, this armor actually becomes a target for missile weapons, and hence so does its wearer. The choice is simple: deadly arrows or deadly swords. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell
– Crushing Damage Resistance: +10%
– Slashing Damage Resistance: +10%
– Piercing Damage Resistance: +10%

Armor Class: 5 (3 vs. slashing, 4 vs. piercing, 15 vs. missile)
Requires:
 6 Strength

Weight: 8"




//RING OF CLUMSINESS//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RING04.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Ring"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "A ring is a small band of precious metal that is used as jewelry. Some rare rings have had enchantments placed upon them that confer various magical abilities. These rings are highly sought after, especially by those of the adventuring profession.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0"

	SAY NAME2 "Ring of Clumsiness"
	SAY DESC "The most notorious owner of this ring made a substantial living exploiting its cursed nature. Gregoria the Foole, a Jester by trade, would use his incomparable sleight of hand to switch this ring with that of a patsy taken from his audience. The rest of his performance would involve the mocking of the newly clumsy individual, much to the delight of their comrades. The ring was removed (by a method known only to the wily Jester) only once the stooge had promised no reprisals for the treatment he had received, though Gregoria frequently still had to make a hasty retreat. What he didn't know was that the ring also held other hidden abilities, which were revealed by an angry mage during her final performance at Zhentil Keep... 


STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Dexterity: -50% penalty
– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell

Charge abilities twice a day:
- Melf's Acid Arrow or Flame Arrow (both at level 10 - 50% chance of each) three times per day

Weight: 0"






//RING OF FOLLY//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/RING23.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Ring"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "A ring is a small band of precious metal that is used as jewelry. Some rare rings have had enchantments placed upon them that confer various magical abilities. These rings are highly sought after, especially by those of the adventuring profession.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 0"

SAY NAME2 "Ring of Folly"
	SAY DESC "Oft the bane of the careless mage, this ring was actually used to promote humility. Hergat Norin, a grand wizard of Narfell, would give the this ring, also known as Discipliner,to his most skilled and most lazy students. Drastically weakening their learning abilities, the ring required all their willpower to unleash its true potential.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Intelligence: -50% penalty
- The wearer can memorize one less spell per level
- Improves casting speed by 2
- Improves caster level by 2

– May only be removed with a Remove Curse spell

Weight: 0 " 



//POTION OF STRENGTH//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/POTN03.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Potion"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Potions are typically found in ceramic, crystal, glass, or metal flasks or vials. Flasks or other containers generally contain enough fluid to provide one person with one complete dose to achieve the effects of the potion.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"


	SAY NAME2 "Potion of Strength"
	SAY DESC "This potion increases the strength of the user. When it is consumed, the individual gains great strength and bonuses to hit and damage while using any hand-held or thrown weapon. The effect lasts for 2 hours.

STATISTICS:

Strength: 18
Duration: 3 hours

Weight: 1" 





//POTION OF EXCEPTIONAL STRENGTH//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/POTN12.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Potion"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Potions are typically found in ceramic, crystal, glass, or metal flasks or vials. Flasks or other containers generally contain enough fluid to provide one person with one complete dose to achieve the effects of the potion.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"


	SAY NAME2 "Potion of Exceptional Strength"
	SAY DESC "This potion increases the strength of the user. When it is consumed, the individual gains great strength and bonuses to hit and damage while using any hand-held or thrown weapon. The effect lasts for 2 hours.

STATISTICS:

Strength: 18/50
Duration: 3 hours

Weight: 1" 





//POTION OF EXTRAORDINARY STRENGTH//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/POTN04.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Potion"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Potions are typically found in ceramic, crystal, glass, or metal flasks or vials. Flasks or other containers generally contain enough fluid to provide one person with one complete dose to achieve the effects of the potion.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 1"


	SAY NAME2 "Potion of Extraordinary Strength"
	SAY DESC "This potion increases the strength of the user. When it is consumed, the individual gains great strength and bonuses to hit and damage while using any hand-held or thrown weapon. The effect lasts for 2 hours.

STATISTICS:

Strength: 18/75
Duration: 3 hours

